  "summary": "Rooted in Eastern Mediterranean traditions, this refreshing <b>Lebanese grain salad</b> offers a vibrant array of textures and bold herbal flavors in a completely plant-based format. Whole roasted green wheat, known as freekeh, serves as the hearty base, offering a smoky nuttiness and chewiness that stands up beautifully to fresh vegetables. Abundant amounts of finely chopped flat-leaf parsley and fresh mint bring an aromatic brightness that defines authentic Levantine salads. Crisp diced cucumber and sweet halved cherry tomatoes add refreshing crunch and juicy moisture, while ruby pomegranate seeds provide bursts of sweet-tart flavor throughout. A light dressing made from extra virgin olive oil and freshly squeezed lemon juice is heightened by sumac, a tangy berry spice with a lemony zip. Topped with buttery toasted walnuts for extra crunch, this wholesome salad can be prepared ahead or enjoyed fresh at room temperature, making it a perfect dish for summer lunches, outdoor gatherings, or healthy meal preparation.",
